# Differentiate deeper. Make decisions differentiable. Math that trains.

omnibias supplies derivative and optimization infrastructure for PINNs and
scientific machine learning. It **solves the nested high-order spatial-autodiff
graph bottleneck on supported paths**: shared activation polynomials, forward
Taylor composition and direct operator contractions replace repeated backward
graphs while retaining gradients into model parameters. This makes demonstrated
high-order residuals practical to train.

Choose the quantity before a general differentiation strategy:

- Activation derivatives use shared Riccati polynomial recurrences and one base
  activation evaluation; total polynomial arithmetic still grows with order.
- Directional jets carry selected directions. Mixed jets carry mixed partials;
  their coefficient count grows combinatorially with dimension and order.
- Ridge and deep Laplacian contractions avoid materializing a full Hessian.
  Deep Laplacians have parameter-gradient regressions at D=5,000 and no fixed
  dimension cap; fixed-width/depth work and memory still grow with dimension.
- Residual derivatives remain trainable tensor expressions. Parameter-curvature
  methods support Newton, Gauss–Newton and structured approximations with their
  distinct assumptions.
- Soft partition gates route into regional experts and propagate gradients into
  thresholds, features and experts: **make decisions differentiable**. Neural
  features and soft trees can train jointly; stagewise GBM-style boosting is a
  separate consumer procedure. A hard discontinuity itself is not differentiated.
- Verified intervals and checked certificates bound supported quantities under
  explicit assumptions. Consumer PINN solvers add boundary, causal, multilevel
  and conditioned-operator methods; those integrations live outside this repo.

Bias collapse (`δ → 0`) extracts derivatives from normalized weighted shifts.
Temperature collapse (`β → ∞`) hardens soft decisions. Keep these limits distinct.
Replacing nested graphs removes their growth mechanism; numerical instability
must still be measured independently. Direct formulas can suffer cancellation,
and shared algebra does not imply universal floating-point identity. These
primitives do not establish convergence for every PDE or solve every training
and approximation difficulty.

